# Threat-hunting project safeguards

Apply only in `ai-enabled-threathunting`. Read current root `AGENTS.md`,
`README.md#current-status` and `docs/operator-runbook.md`. Use installed global
`agentic-security-workflows` with its threat-hunting reference for shared principles.
Documentation does not change the active engine, execution scope, limits or
approval requirements and does not authorize deployment, access or external action.

For report/browser/export changes, use the local `threat-hunt-reporting` skill and
current `docs/threat-hunt-reporting-guidance.md`. Preserve saved content, analyst
edits, evidence identity, finalization guards and immutable historical PDFs.
Test at desktop viewport sizes only unless the user explicitly requests mobile
work. Preserve historical mobile evidence without rerunning it. Use current
runbook/context for local operations; no second global learning store.
